    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes the Humming load crash for per-tensor FP8 MoE checkpoints, which currently fails the `Qwen3-30B-A3B-Fp8-v1-humming` and `Qwen3-30B-A3B-Fp8-v1-humming-act-fp8` LM Eval configs on main (seen in the B200 and H100 Humming jobs on #60948). Regressed in #56997.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Per-tensor FP8 MoE with `--moe-backend humming` loads again instead of failing engine init with `assert scale.size(0) == (num_experts or 1)`.\n- The fix covers every producer that requantizes w13 to one scale per expert (compressed-tensors, `fp8`, ModelOpt, online FP8). Block, channel and MXFP8 scales and non-gated MoE are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n`nm-testing/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Fp8-v1` with `--moe-backend humming --linear-backend humming --enforce-eager` on SM80:\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Engine init | `AssertionError` in `humming/schema/base.py` | loads |\n| `Qwen3-30B-A3B-Fp8-v1-humming` GSM8K (1319 q, 5-shot, threshold 0.86) | crash | 0.8787, passed |\n\n```bash\ncd tests\npytest -s -v evals/gsm8k/test_gsm8k_correctness.py --config-list-file=<list containing Qwen3-30B-A3B-Fp8-v1-humming.yaml>\n```\n\nThe `-act-fp8` config needs FP8 activations, which Humming rejects on SM80 by design. Locally it now gets past the weight conversion (w13 converts to a channel scale) and stops at that input-schema check, so its accuracy is left to the H100/B200 Humming jobs.\n\n## Details\n\nSince #56997, the Humming branch of `convert_to_fp8_moe_kernel_format` writes the processed tensors back to the layer before the Humming conversion. For per-tensor FP8, `process_fp8_weight_tensor_strategy_moe` has already requantized w13 to the max scale of each expert, so the layer now holds a `[E]` w13 scale. Humming's per-tensor schema expects one scale per gate/up shard: with two n-stacks it views the scale as `(-1, 2, 1)`, which turns `[E]` into `[E/2, 2, 1]` and trips the assertion.\n\nDropping the write-back would bring back the old pairing of requantized weights with the per-shard checkpoint scales. Instead this repeats the requantized scale for both shards, which matches the requantized weight exactly. `numel == num_experts` only holds for per-tensor scales, and non-gated w13 keeps a single n-stack. The existing Humming LM Eval configs already cover this path, so no new test.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance: Claude\n",
